      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m a bit concerned about making the backends return partially initialized BGs because creating them from the frontend data is solely their responsibility, and the backend BG/BGLs need to know that the creation is done entirely in this scope and not potentially deferred to later.\n\nIn D3D12 the init would be called in https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/d3d12/BindGroupD3D12.cpp;drc\u003d20799f4c32d950ce93d495f44eec648400f38a19;l\u003d49\n\nIn Vulkan in https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/vulkan/BindGroupVk.cpp;drc\u003dc40228e6fc111f23b96cfb0be7672e47b64e9168;l\u003d47\n\nIn Metal we\u0027d introduce a similar function here https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/metal/BindGroupMTL.mm;drc\u003dcc2516ac15ebeb6c3c07a427a76d6b57832d3154;l\u003d34\n\netc. This would also match how all the other objects are handled in the backends.",
      "revId": "46fb413ea553b235d664dd3a13cb585a7f6f5428",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
